  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes (especially after sentiment > 0.00).",
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is consistently negative (sentiment < 0.00) or near-zero (sentiment = 0.00) over recent days.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above recent 7-day average, reduce by 5-10% for next period.",
    "Increase downward bias when sentiment is positive (sentiment > 0.00) and true outcome is trending lower.",
    "Lag correction: if true outcome is below forecast by > 5% for 3+ consecutive days, reduce next forecast by 3-5%.",
    "Avoid overreacting to single-day sentiment spikes — smooth sentiment transitions before adjusting forecasts."
  ]
}
